      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:3:132:2",
      "text": [
        " سَمِعْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) يَقُولُ إِنَّمَا يُكْرَهُ الْقِرَانُ فِي الْفَرِيضَةِ فَأَمَّا النَّافِلَةُ فَلَا وَ اللَّهِ مَا بِهِ بَأْسٌ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Muhammad Bin Ahmad Al Nahdy, from Muhammad Bin Waleed, from Umar Bin Yazeed who said, ",
          "‘I heard Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> saying: ‘But rather the pairing during the Obligatory (<span class=\"iTxt\">Tawaaf</span>) is disliked. But, as for the optional, so no, by Allah<sup>azwj</sup>, there is no problem with it’."
        ]
      }
